[PARKED 2026-08-08 -- CONFIG_USB_SUNXI_DMA is OFF, this patch is inert.]

Kept on purpose rather than dropped: MUSB DMA does not work on this silicon and
is slower than the PIO it replaces, but the failure is partly a documentation
problem, so this stays in the series in case better material on the suniv MUSB
DMA path appears. Guarded by #ifdef CONFIG_USB_SUNXI_DMA and falls back to
mainline's NULL stubs, so the tree builds clean with the option off.

Measured on hardware, kernel 6.18.42:
  storage 64 MiB  PIO 10.05 MiB/s, 10.03 cs/MiB | DDMA 3.28 MiB/s, 29.17 cs/MiB
  wired CarPlay   PIO full session, 28-30 fps   | DDMA never establishes at all
Why, and how to revive it: docs/musb-dma-fix-plan.md

lctech f1c200s: wire the MUSB (usb_otg) node to the dedicated-DMA engine

Add dmas/dma-names to usb@1c13000 so sunxi_dma.c (CONFIG_USB_SUNXI_DMA) can
request the DDMA USB DRQ (SUN4I_DMA_DEDICATED 4) for the RX and TX endpoint
FIFO paths. This is the DDMA bank (channels distinct from esp-hosted's SPI
NDMA), so USB and SPI DMA do not share channels.

Depends on patch 0014 (adds the &dma controller node + the sun4i-a10.h
dt-binding include).

Signed-off-by: mbt28 <btekbas@gmail.com>

--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c100s.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/allwinner/suniv-f1c100s.dtsi
@@ -145,6 +145,9 @@
 			phy-names = "usb";
 			extcon = <&usbphy 0>;
 			allwinner,sram = <&otg_sram 1>;
+			dmas = <&dma SUN4I_DMA_DEDICATED 4>,
+			       <&dma SUN4I_DMA_DEDICATED 4>;
+			dma-names = "rx", "tx";
 			status = "disabled";
 		};
 
